        "node_id": "n_4_d537bc",
        "thought_text": "The current approach iterates over each word in the dictionary, removing it temporarily and recalculating the shortest path. This is computationally expensive and may lead to incorrect results due to the way the BFS is implemented. Instead, consider generating all possible one-letter transformations of the start and end words and checking if they can be connected using the existing dictionary plus the newly added word.",
